    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1076">

                <pb facs="0985" n="671" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg671"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the German Chargé
                        d’Affaires</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Haniel</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-17">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 17, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>It is expected question concerning wireless will be settled tomorrow. Department
                    advised that no license for operation of Tuckerton station has been taken out
                    under the act of August 13, 1912.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
